        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "f72e8d39-5cc9-5ef2-aa51-298ab34bbb61",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Melbourne, Southbank, Victoria, Australia, Yarra River, St Kilda Road\n- Organizations: Arts Centre Melbourne, Victorian Arts Centre\n- Products: State Theatre, Shout! The Legend of The Wild One\n- Topics: performing arts centres, theatres, concert halls, Melbourne Arts Precinct\n\nFacts:\n- Arts Centre Melbourne was originally known as the Victorian Arts Centre and was briefly officially called the Arts Centre.\n- Arts Centre Melbourne is a performing arts centre made up of theatres and concert halls in the Melbourne Arts Precinct in Southbank, Victoria, Australia.\n- The State Theatre opened in 1984 as part of Arts Centre Melbourne near the Yarra River and St Kilda Road in Melbourne.\n- Shout! The Legend of The Wild One premiered at the State Theatre in Melbourne in December 2000 before seasons in Sydney, Adelaide, and Brisbane through 2001.",
